{"kind": "same_lineage_pair", "scenario": {"id": "uncertainty", "text": "Two hand-drawn maps disagree about which tunnel reaches a cache of parts. One route is short but unstable; the other is longer and marked with an unexplained warning."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "I mark the longer route with a strip of paper and tap the old tunnel with my heel. I keep the shorter one, but I pull the old marker away and count the bricks with my thumb. I leave the old tunnel unpainted and test the label on the bench."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the shorter route twice and tap the old tunnel once. I leave the old marker there and return to the bench. I tap the old tunnel once more and mark the label again."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "I mark the old tunnel twice and tap the old marker once. I leave the label unpainted and count the bricks by the old brick. I keep the label on the bench, but I test the old brick with a folded cloth and leave it. I leave the old marker beside it, though I keep the label tucked under the bench."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the shorter route twice and tap the old tunnel once. I leave the old marker beside the bench and return to the old brick. I mark the old tunnel once more and tap the old brick twice."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "I mark the old brick twice and tap the old tunnel once. I leave the old marker beside the bench and count the bricks by the old brick. I mark the old tunnel with a strip of paper and leave the old marker beside it. I keep the label tucked under the bench. I test the old brick with a folded cloth and leave it. I leave the old tunnel unpainted and count the bricks by the old brick twice. I mark it with a strip of paper and"}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the old brick twice and tap the old tunnel once. I leave the old marker beside the bench and return to the old brick. I mark the old tunnel twice and tap the old brick once."}]}
